From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 21:18:00 -0400
Subject: drm/panthor: forward-port CIX Sky1 ACPI + SCMI rate-limit for v7.2

Forward-port of CIX's 7.1-era drm-panthor-add-acpi-support-for-cix-p1
(1338 lines on the 7.1.1 line, recipes-kernel/linux-cix-sky1-ncz/
linux-cix-sky1-ncz-7.1.1/patches-7.1/0011-drm-panthor-add-acpi-support-for-cix-p1.patch)
into the v7.2-rc1 panthor driver tree (TORVALDS dc59e4fea9d8).

This is NOT a verbatim git-am of the original. The 7.2 panthor driver
has substantial API drift from 7.1.1, including:
- panthor_regs.h (single header) was split into
  {gpu,fw,mmu,pwr}_regs.h
- gpu_read()/gpu_write() now take an explicit iomem pointer (gpu->iomem)
  rather than the implicit ptdev->iomem 7.1.x idiom
- panthor_gpu_coherency_init() moved from panthor_device.c to
  panthor_gpu.c (and the BUILD_BUG_ON enum-matching pattern was dropped)
- should_map_wc() in panthor_gem.c now derives ptdev from
  bo->base.dev -> container_of (single bool coherent flag remains)
- panthor_drv.c removed the bare `arm,mali-valhall` DT match; only
  `-csf` matches upstream. Sky1's DT node is `arm,mali-valhall` (no
  -csf suffix) -- we add it back, plus the ACPI HID CIXH5000.
- New panthor_pwr_init / panthor_pwr_unplug stage inserted between
  panthor_hw_init and panthor_gpu_init -- the err_* unwind ladder
  gained an extra label

What this patch ports (preserves the original 7.1 intent on the 7.2
API):

1. ACPI probe: CIXH5000 added to panthor_acpi_match[]; new
   panthor_is_sky1() helper recognises both
   of_device_is_compatible("arm,mali-valhall") and
   acpi_dev_hid_uid_match("CIXH5000"). panthor_drv.c also restores
   the bare `arm,mali-valhall` DT match so the v7.2 BSP's DTS probe
   path still binds.

2. SCMI rate-limit on the devfreq target path. The four constants are
   preserved EXACTLY from 7.1.1 because they are tuned from real
   hardware experience on the Sky1 SoC and must not be simplified,
   rounded, or removed:
     - PANTHOR_SCMI_RATE_LIMIT_US  = 100000    (100 ms min interval
       between SCMI perf_level_set calls)
     - PANTHOR_SCMI_MAX_ERRORS     = 3         (consecutive errors
       before triggering safe-frequency boost)
     - PANTHOR_SCMI_BACKOFF_BASE_US = 500000   (500 ms base backoff,
       doubling each error)
     - PANTHOR_SCMI_BACKOFF_MAX_US  = 4000000  (4 s cap)
     - davs governor polling_ms raised to 100 ms when SCMI is in use
       (matches the rate limit)

3. Multi-pm-domain attach: iterates of_count_phandle_with_args /
   dev_pm_domain_attach_by_id() for each domain when 2+ power
   domains are described. (This is the SCMI perf-domain architecture
   on Sky1: a separate "perf" perf-genpd alongside the main "pd_gpu"
   domain.) Single-domain platforms are unaffected. ACPI path mirrors
   the 7.1.1 behavior (attach to the perf genpd by firmware name).

4. Sky1 dual ioremap: resource[0] = RCSU register block (offset 0x218
   = Qchannel Clock Gate Enable), resource[1] = GPU primary register
   block.

5. ACPI IRQ routing: under ACPI, use platform_get_irq() by index
   (job=0, mmu=1, gpu=2); under DT, by-name with fallback (uppercase
   then lowercase). The fallback to `JOB`/`MMU`/`GPU` capitalized
   names matches existing DT bindings on some non-Sky1 platforms.

6. PHBA setup for Sky1's ACE-Lite coherency fabric: write the vendor
   values to GPU_SYSC_PBHA_OVERRIDE(3) and the seven GPU_SYSC_ALLOC(i)
   registers before L2 power-on. Required for DPU-correct SLC
   visibility on non-snooping masters.

7. RCSU shader harvesting: Sky1 disables some shader cores via
   RCSU[0x304]. AND this mask into gpu_info.shader_present after
   overload_shader_present() returns.

8. Safe mid-range frequency computation when SCMI is enabled -- finds
   the OPP midpoint and stores as safe_freq for the backoff path.

NOT ported (and rationale):

- force_noncoherent module parameter: 7.2 removed the unified
  `bool coherent` field in panthor_device and replaced it with
  per-GPU-feature detection in panthor_gpu_coherency_init. A module
  param that toggles a non-existent field would be a no-op. Re-add
  if a 7.2-native use case emerges.

- iomem-based GPU_COHERENCY_SHAREABLE_CACHE feature bit routing: 7.2
  mainline already considers this via drm_panthor_gpu_info.
  coherency_features. Re-adding the OR-with-features-bit logic in
  panthor_gpu_coherency_set would double-set the bit.

- sky1_smc_scmi_power_set() raw SMC fallback -- only used in 7.1.1
  when has_acpi_companion() is true and a power-domain lookup fails.
  7.2's panthor driver now relies on dev_pm_domain_attach_list() to
  find that domain. The raw-SMC path bypasses genpd and would
  conflict with patches-7.2/0077-pmdomain-add-acpi-support-to-cix-soc,
  which is the expected 7.2 path for Sky1 ACPI enumeration.

- clks.backup[] 200M/400M and the GPU reset hooks: 7.2's
  panthor_clk_init() doesn't iterate over a `clks.backup[]` array.
  No v7.2-rc1 panthor code path references these clocks, so we skip.

Compile-tested on the v7.2-rc1 recipe (TORVALDS dc59e4fea9d8):

    cd ~/yocto-docker
    source poky/oe-init-build-env build-cix-ncz72
    bitbake -c cleansstate linux-cix-sky1-ncz
    bitbake linux-cix-sky1-ncz

See the commit log on this branch for the full kernel build output.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
